anaging Training and Development Overview Managing Employee Development Supervisor Training and Development Team and Organizational Development Compensation Managing Workplace Concerns show submenu for Managing Workplace Concerns Managing Workplace Concerns Overview Reporting Discrimination, Harassment or Retaliation Staff and Faculty Relations Services Staff Misconduct Faculty Misconduct Drug and Alcohol Testing Managing Transition and Separation Benefits and Wellness show submenu for Benefits and Wellness Benefits and Wellness Overview Employee Discounts and Perks State Insurance Benefit Plans show submenu for State Insurance Benefit Plans State Insurance Benefit Plans Overview Your Employee Benefits Package State Insurance Plan Options Interactive Benefits Overview PEBA MyBenefits Login PEBA Health Perks and Resources Retirement Changes: Major Life Events show submenu for Changes: Major Life Events Changes: Major Life Events Overview Resources for Pregnancy, Childbirth and Related Conditions Holidays and Leave show submenu for Holidays and Leave Holidays and Leave Overview Holiday Schedule Summary of Leave Benefits Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Kronos Information Employee Assistance Program Employee Wellness show submenu for Employee Wellness Employee Wellness Overview Financial Wellness Clemson Rural Health Campus Recreation Outdoor Wellness Activities Employee Tuition Assistance Program Logins and Resources show submenu for Logins and Resources Logins and Resources Overview Logins show submenu for Logins Logins Overview Workday Tiger Training OnBase-Performance Contact HR HR Service Center Forms and Resource Library Policies and Procedures Employment Verification Payroll Timekeeping Information Clemson Home Office of Human Resources Current: Careers From our first graduating class in 1896 to today, Clemson University has become a leader in higher education by setting records in student success, research, outreach, athletics, fundraising, industry partnerships, innovation and impact. We promote a championship culture across our campuses, and our dedicated faculty, staff, and students contribute to the success of each other. As we continue to elevate Clemson, we seek ambitious, talented professionals who want to join our team. So, let's get started today! Are you ready to answer the call? Staff Positions (current employees) Staff Positions (external candidates) Faculty Positions Student Employment Clemson University Foundation Positions IPTAY Positions Why Choose Clemson? One of the most productive public research universities in the nation, Clemson University attracts and powerfully unites students, faculty and staff whose greatest desire is to make a difference in the lives of others. Classified as an R1 – Very High Research University by Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education – Clemson is dedicated to teaching, research and service. We are guided by our bold strategic plan, Clemson Elevate, which seeks to propel Clemson’s success and further strengthen our reputation. With you on our team, we will deliver the No. 1 student experience, double research by 2035 and transform lives statewide and beyond. “ “Clemson's focus is on the people, be it students, staff, faculty or visitors. That's what I love most about being part of this amazing University.” Candice Heatherly Administrative Officer College of Agriculture, Forestry and Life Sciences The Benefits of Being a Tiger Life is good in Clemson At Clemson, we place an emphasis on a positive experience for members of the Clemson Family! Learn more about all Clemson has to offer for faculty and staff. Why Choose Clemson A great place to live and work! Build a future in Clemson Clemson is not only a great place to work – it is a great place to live, play and discover! Learn more about living in the Upstate of South Carolina. Living in the Upstate University News “ “Clemson’s energy and ambition are palpable. It’s exciting to be part of a University on the rise, where innovative research, teaching and outreach are respected, supported and rewarded.” Joseph Ura Professor and Chair Department of Political Science Supporting Our Faculty and Staff At Clemson, we pride ourselves in supporting our faculty and staff members and we look forward to supporting you on your journey to Clemson! Check out some of our perks and benefits of Clemson employment below. Training and Development Employee Wellness Tuition Assistance Program Supporting Our Military Notice (Clery Act) The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available to view and download on the CUPD Annual Reports webpage . Notice of Filing Labor Condition Application (LCA) In compliance with the U.S. Department of Labor requirements, employers petitioning for non-immigrant work visas must post employment details relevant to the LCA for ten business days. The linked postings reference positions for which Clemson University intends to hire non-immigrant employees under the classification of H-1B or E-3 specialty workers. Candidates have already been selected to fill the positions below. The “Notice of Filing a Labor Condition Application” is not a posting for an open position. Office of Human Resources Copyright © Clemson University Office of Human Resources | 108 Perimeter Rd, Clemson, SC 29634 Contact Us intro-arrow Engage With Us Through Instagram - Office of Human Resources Twitter - Office of Human Resources LinkedIn - Office of Human Resources Clemson University Facebook Instagram Twitter/X Linkedin Youtube Policy Accessibility Title IX Non-Discrimination & Anti-Harassment Policy Ethics/Safety\n    \t\t\t\t\t\t\tHotline Privacy Statement Copyright © 2026 Clemson University • Clemson, South Carolina 29634 Clemson University Clemson University Facebook Clemson University Instagram Clemson University Twitter/X Clemson University Linkedin Clemson University Youtube Resources A-Z Index Campus Map CU Safety Directory Webcams Apply to\n    \t\t\t\t\t\t\tClemson"
