 workforce! The SkillBridge program (PDF) is an opportunity for service members to gain valuable civilian work experience through specific industry training, apprenticeships or internships during the last 180 days of service. DOD SkillBridge provides an invaluable chance for service members to work and learn in civilian career areas. Service members participating in the DOD SkillBridge at Clemson continue receiving their military compensation and benefits, while receiving civilian training and work experience. Get started below! Contact the Talent Acquisition Team Quick Links DOD SkillBridge Website O*Net Online Military Crosswalk Search Clemson’s Military Heritage Supporting Our Military Employees SkillBridge FAQ For Service Members Ready to take the next step? It is a great time to be a Clemson Tiger! If you are interested in applying to be a SkillBridge intern at Clemson, please select the button below to fill out a SkillBridge Request form. Apply Today! For Clemson Hiring Managers Want to get involved with SkillBridge? Are you interested in hosting a SkillBridge Intern? Use the form below to register your department as a Clemson SkillBridge partner. Register Today! Office of Human Resources Copyright © Clemson University Office of Human Resources | 108 Perimeter Rd, Clemson, SC 29634 Contact Us intro-arrow Engage With Us Through Instagram - Office of Human Resources Twitter - Office of Human Resources LinkedIn - Office of Human Resources Clemson University Facebook Instagram Twitter/X Linkedin Youtube Policy Accessibility Title IX Non-Discrimination & Anti-Harassment Policy Ethics/Safety\n    \t\t\t\t\t\t\tHotline Privacy Statement Copyright © 2026 Clemson University • Clemson, South Carolina 29634 Clemson University Clemson University Facebook Clemson University Instagram Clemson University Twitter/X Clemson University Linkedin Clemson University Youtube Resources A-Z Index Campus Map CU Safety Directory Webcams Apply to\n    \t\t\t\t\t\t\tClemson"
